// ============================================================================
// _probes.kql — one-off schema probes for this chapter
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Run each block once in Advanced Hunting and note the answer next to it.
// Queries reference these as P1..P9 in their headers. None change anything.
// ============================================================================

// ---- P1: EntraIdSignInEvents schema ------------------------------------------
// Gates: incident/4 (country column name to restore geo context; confirm
//        ErrorCode and RiskLevelDuringSignIn exist under these names).
// EntraIdSignInEvents | getschema
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): country column = ____________

// ---- P2: EmailPostDeliveryEvents action vocabulary ----------------------------
// Gates: incident/3 and detection/3 ("ZAP"/"delete" has-matching; also any
//        future remediation-efficacy metrics).
// EmailPostDeliveryEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(7d)
// | summarize count() by ActionType, Action, ActionResult
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): ____________

// ---- P3: EmailDirection of internal SPO share notifications --------------------
// Gates: incident/5 (its mail leg deliberately has no direction filter).
//        Have a colleague share a file with you, then:
// EmailEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(1d)
// | where SenderFromAddress =~ "no-reply@sharepointonline.com"
// | where Subject has "shared"
// | project Timestamp, EmailDirection, Subject, RecipientEmailAddress
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): internal shares classify as = ____________

// ---- P4: CloudAppEvents AccountId shape for Exchange/SharePoint audit ----------
// Gates: incident/4 (inbox-rule leg assumes AccountId carries the UPN;
//        share-op leg assumes RawEventData.UserId does).
// CloudAppEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(7d)
// | where ActionType in ("New-InboxRule", "Set-InboxRule", "UpdateInboxRules")
// | project Timestamp, ActionType, AccountId, AccountDisplayName, RawEventData
// | take 10
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): AccountId is UPN? ____________

// ---- P5: CloudAppEvents mailbox-persistence action vocabulary ------------------
// Gates: incident/4 (mailbox leg beyond inbox rules: forwarding via
//        Set-Mailbox — parameter names expected as tokens in RawEventData —
//        and permission grants under these ActionType names).
// CloudAppEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(30d)
// | where ActionType in ("Set-Mailbox", "Add-MailboxPermission",
//                        "Add-RecipientPermission", "Remove-InboxRule",
//                        "Disable-InboxRule")
// | summarize count() by ActionType
// | union (CloudAppEvents
//     | where Timestamp > ago(30d)
//     | where ActionType == "Set-Mailbox"
//     | where RawEventData has_any ("ForwardingSmtpAddress", "ForwardingAddress",
//                                   "DeliverToMailboxAndForward")
//     | take 5 | project ActionType = strcat("fwd-sample: ", tostring(RawEventData)))
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): action types present = ____________ fwd params visible? ____________

// ---- P6: EntraIdSignInEvents SessionId population ------------------------------
// Gates: incident/4 (session-anomaly leg: one SessionId seen from multiple
//        IPs) and incident/6 (SessionId reuse as the stronger pivot than IP).
//        If SessionId is blank in this tenant, both degrade to IP reasoning.
// EntraIdSignInEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(7d)
// | summarize Total = count(), WithSession = countif(isnotempty(SessionId))
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): populated for ____ % of sign-ins

// ---- P7: Entra audit vocabulary in CloudAppEvents ------------------------------
// Gates: incident/4 and 3b — the auth-method, OAuth-consent and
//        device-registration legs match ActionType strings that are NOT yet
//        verified in this tenant. If the real strings differ, those legs
//        return empty and FAIL SILENT. Compare output against the lists in 4.
// CloudAppEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(30d)
// | where ActionType has_any ("security info", "Consent", "PermissionGrant",
//                             "service principal", "device", "password",
//                             "application")
// | summarize count() by Application, ActionType
// | sort by count_ desc
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): auth-method strings = ______ consent strings = ______
//                      device strings = ______

// ---- P8: UPN vs primary SMTP divergence ----------------------------------------
// Gates: incident/4 and 3b (idMap / addrToUpn resolution). If UPN == primary
//        SMTP for every account the resolution is a harmless no-op; where
//        they diverge it is what keeps the mail legs from silently missing.
// IdentityInfo
// | where isnotempty(AccountUpn) and isnotempty(EmailAddress)
// | summarize arg_max(Timestamp, EmailAddress) by AccountUpn
// | summarize Accounts = count(),
//             Diverging = countif(tolower(AccountUpn) != tolower(EmailAddress))
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): ____ of ____ accounts diverge

// ---- P9: UrlClickEvents.UrlChain population ------------------------------------
// Gates: incident/7 section 1 (redirect chain recorded at click time — the
//        cheapest source for the second-stage / harvest host).
// UrlClickEvents
// | where Timestamp > ago(7d)
// | summarize Total = count(), WithChain = countif(isnotempty(UrlChain))
// ANSWER (YYYY-MM-DD): populated? ____________
